  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMPALA: Improving Model Processes for African cLimAte</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMPALA will deliver a step change in global model climate prediction for Africa on the 5-40 year timescale by delivering reductions in model systematic errors, resulting in reduced uncertainty in predictions of African climate and enabling improved assessment of the robustness of multi-model projections for the continent. 
The ultimate beneficiaries of the research will be people of the sub-Saharan Africa region, and IMPALA scientists will assist in generating cross-programme outputs, such as material demonstrating improved capability to assess risks of key agriculture-relevant rainfall events, for their user training workshops and interactions with other DFID programmes, and broader capacity development and adaptation activities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research and development activity contributing to the UK&#x2019;s strategy to address key development challenges.</narrative>
